bodyHtml: |
  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Seyne-sur-Mer has banned dogs, even on a leash, from its Saint-Elme, Sablettes, Mar-Vivo and Fabrégas beaches since the 2012 order, under penalty of a fine of up to €150 (la-seyne.fr). Toutou Beach, created in 2022 at Saint-Elme, is the dog swimming area provided by the city.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>According to the city, Toutou Beach is at the very end of the Saint-Elme harbour, just past the diving club. The order governing it only allows dogs on a leash, muzzled for category 2 dogs; category 1 dogs are banned. Dogs may not be made to play or run on the beach or in the water, and use of the site must not obstruct users of the neighbouring boat launch ramp. The area is open year-round at the hours given by the Provence Méditerranée tourist office. Local residents' appeal against the order was reported by the press in March 2025: we found no decision, and the city's page still presents the area.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: don't settle on another La Seyne beach thinking "it's the same": the ban there is enforced with fines.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Saint-Elme harbour and the boat launch ramp are next door; the nearby Sablettes are off-limits to dogs.</p>
